                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_EPS.BV.BV_EPS.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTC_0xD30F81">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTC_0xD30F81</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>13832065</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>U130F81</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1876940853">Keys [Symmetric key/Key-Raw] corrupted</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>3</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1579948055">depend on vehicle </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1750069931">Check Key value</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_380212341"> - Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V) 
 - PwrMod == IGN ON
 - BUS physical status</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_533095110">During Start up &amp; Key Load</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1395450602">The component shall set the DTC Immediately if any of the below listed conditions occurs:
(a) Key Storage into Memory Failed (Example Encryption failed)
(b) Key retrieval from Memory Failed (Example  CRC/Checksum/Hash/Decryption failed)
(c) All bytes of Raw_Key are either 0x00 (initial value) or 0xFF.
(d) Loading the Key to HSM or equivalent function failed.

The Failure will be latched (i.e. Entire ECU power cycle) until valid keys are updated.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1882495731">The component shall not set any DTC if the ECU is able to read and write the key-raw successfully from it's memory</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_298787442">Normal Assist</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1203974766">40 dec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_670929328">ECU cannot read and write the key-raw successfully from it's memory</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1038443173">Normal assist, Key verfication fail</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_EPS.BV.BV_EPS.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTC_0xD31086">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTC_0xD31086</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>13832326</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>U131086</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1654870846">MAC Generation/Verification Fail</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>3</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1579948055">depend on vehicle </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_222090655">Check MAC Generation or verification</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_380212341"> - Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V) 
 - PwrMod == IGN ON
 - BUS physical status</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_426872011">failure to authenticate at any time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1243425472">The component shall set the DTC If
- secured pdu can't be verified within 0.7 ms (main frequency:80MHz)  
OR
If MAC Generation or verification fails for 3 consecutive messages.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_599137725">The component shall clear the DTC immediately If MAC Generation/Verification is successful once.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_298787442">Normal Assist</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1203974766">40 dec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_825588580">GW generation or EPS verification fail</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_298787442">Normal Assist</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_EPS.BV.BV_EPS.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTC_0xD31185">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTC_0xD31185</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>13832581</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>U131185</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1083951406">Trip/Reset/Message Counters and Reset Flag Range Check Failures.</TEXT>
                                    <LEVEL>3</LEVEL>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1579948055">depend on vehicle </SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_2097459212">Check Trip/Reset/Message Counters and Reset Flag Range</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_380212341"> - Local voltage is within normal range (9-16V) 
 - PwrMod == IGN ON
 - BUS physical status</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_426872011">failure to authenticate at any time</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_666844146">The component shall set the DTC If
- Reset/Message Counter reaches its Maximum value or When an increment condition of the Reset/Message counter occurs at the maximum value of the Reset/Message counter.
OR 
- Abnormal freshness value synchronization message is received (if received freshness values are not within tolerance value); The tolerance value is considered as 3.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_814694139">The component shall clear the DTC immediately If Trip/Reset/Message Counters and Reset Flag are within its Ranges.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_298787442">Normal Assist</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1203974766">40 dec</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_696852070">Trip/Reset/Message Counters and Reset Flag are out of range</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_298787442">Normal Assist</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DLC.DLC_EPS.BV.BV_EPS.DOP.DD_DTCList.DTC.DTC_0xD31281">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTC_0xD31281</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>13832833</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>U131281</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
